Need ensure final boxed answer not just value? I can put:
\boxed{\frac{8}{17}}
and then "attained by...". The instruction "put your final answer within \boxed{}" might be interpreted as the final result. To be safe, final line:
\boxed{\max |f(1/2)|=\frac{8}{17},\text{ attained by }f(z)=\frac{1+4z^2}{4+z^2}}
This includes example in box. Maybe too wide but okay.

Potential alternative: If f has zeros at i/2 and -i/2, maybe can use a version of the Schwarz lemma for functions vanishing at two points: 
|f(z)| ≤ \frac{\prod |z-a_k|}{\prod |1-\bar a_k z|}
provided f maps D to D. This is exactly.
